        "content": [
          "You've now met all six of Toki",
          "Pona's small closing prepositions:",
          "",
          "lon = at, in, during",
          "mi lon tomo. = I'm in the house.",
          "",
          "tawa = to, toward, for",
          "tan = from, because of",
          "kepeken = using, by means of",
          "sama = same as, like",
          "poka = beside, near",
          "",
          "mi lon poka sina.",
          "= I'm right next to you."
        ],
        "pronunciation": "mi lon poka sina"
      },
      {
        "page": 2,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "Comparison works by juxtaposition:",
          "",
          "soweli suli li wawa mute.",
          "soweli lili li wawa lili.",
          "= The big animal is very strong;",
          "the small one, only a little.",
          "",
          "(tan for 'more...than' is used by",
          "some, but collides with tan's core",
          "'from, because of' sense.)",
          "",
          "All six can close a sentence alone,",
          "as the whole predicate:",
          "",
          "mi lon.  = I'm here, I'm present.",
          "mi tawa. = I'm going, I'm off."
        ],
        "pronunciation": "mi tawa"
      }
    ]
  }
